{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And He afflicted you.</b> On the way, as it is written: ״ענה בדרך כחי״." "<b>And He made you hungry.</b> In that He did not give you manna except for each day's portion on its day, and this is <b>and He made you hungry</b> — for one who has bread in his basket is not like one who has no bread in his basket. Another interpretation: <b>and He made you hungry</b> — for had He brought down manna for you while you were still sated from the provisions that you had in your hand, which you brought out of Egypt, you would not have paid attention to it, even to taste it, for you would not have abandoned the bread you were accustomed to in favor of <b>manna which you did not know, nor did your fathers know</b>. Therefore He made you hungry."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:52:07.472046542Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}